/-!
# Exact order exclusions for the small SL₃(3) nodes

The finite lists certify the exact orders of the twenty-one nontrivial nodes
whose orders are not divisible by four. The trivial node is handled directly.
Each count uses the rooted generator and closure certificates of `Listing`;
no order inferred from the earlier coset covers is used. The conjunction of
checks is elaborated sequentially to bound memory use.

Witness generator: `MatrixClassification/source/generate.py`.
Source application: Bender (1974), (4.1), p.225, citing Janko (1966), Lemma 3.1.
-/

